  "compatibilityFindings": [
    "All 15 production Family TypeScript files and activation, runtime-execution, encoder/protocol-leg encoding are byte-identical to the historical accepted source commit. Exact methods, A-state guard, identity, ABI, amounts and caller-only execution unchanged.",
    "RuntimeAmountProgram old constants, load/equality/math0..6 and ordinary call0/static1 byte serialization are unchanged. Added math7/8, callmode2, nested op8 and settlement program dispatch are not emitted by this Family.",
    "Issuer additions map omitted settlement to undefined and compare undefined echo; this Family retains no direct/deferred capability. Original caller/ownership/source fences remain. Quoted tolerance optional field is not read by Curve LP.",
    "All supported LP routes are ordinary ERC20. executionNativeSides returns null and common asset boundary returns original leg; shared native default1 tolerance and native settlement logic are unreachable.",
    "Old artifact exact bytes a2fa2279 reauthenticated against both raw reports. Owner100...1 patch yields recorded a7658a48 runtime. Its four Solidity metadata keccak hashes equal source at historical commit, not a guessed sibling artifact.",
    "Current RuntimeAmountVM introduces context/error diagnostics and additional opcodes/read-only/nesting modes. Original default entry uses readOnly=false/depth0. LP programs use old instructions/call modes and no callbacks; these paths preserve success semantics and revert fail-closed. Diagnostic error envelope changes do not turn any old rejection into success.",
    "Original whole-loop runtime input/output/safety semantics remain; old LP evidence is 48 single-leg positive and32 declared EVM reverts, not a final loop/profit proof. Reauthentication recomputed48 exact debit/output/supply/native and96Transfer log deltas against raw trusted results."
  ],
